import OddPerfect.ExcessFourReduction
import OddPerfect.TwoExcEngineTail

/-!
# Total excess at least 4: exclusion S2a

Let `N` be an odd perfect number with special prime `q` and exponent 4 at 3, at most two further
primes `r₁`, `r₂` of exponent 4, every other prime factor except `q` of exponent 2. This module
proves that no such `N` exists (`excessS2a : ExcessS2a`, the statement of
`ExcessFourReduction`). This concerns only this restricted family, not odd perfect numbers in
general. Every index in this family is 3 or 5 and 3 divides N, so this exclusion also follows
from the published theorem of Fletcher, Nielsen and Ochem (Math. Comp. 81, 2012); it is proved
here independently by a kernel checked certificate.

## The proof

The proof is a kernel checked certificate for the checker `checkV` of `OddPerfect.TwoExcEngine`,
a tool whose soundness theorem `checkV_sound` is proved in `TwoExcEngineCheck` and
`TwoExcEngineTail` (`defSound`). The certificate `cert_ex_S2a_100000_nojump_nolanded.jsonl`
(sha256 `ddd47311c212c627096df16af4b99d9ff29ad812f917f6171469c0ebb6056b43`, 362 lines) is the
output of an exact search. The checker parameters allow 3 exceptional primes (the prime 3 is a
key of exact exponent 4 and counts as one of them), every exception other than 3 of exponent
exactly 4, and do not use the landed facts. As a checker term it has 213 records, 137
contradiction leaves, 20 abundant leaves, 1 deficient leaf, and 54 forced nodes, 2 closed nodes,
146 decide nodes, 1 exponent split. The term is checked in one kernel evaluation; primality
enters only through the verified oracle `prS2a`, which the checker asks about 68 primes (30
below 4096, covered by the verified table `primeB`; the others by one flat Pratt certificate of
70 entries and a search tree over its primes). The bridge `famV_S2a` turns the hypotheses of
`ExcessS2a` into the family of the parameters.

Generated by `gen_excess.py` from `cert_ex_S2a_100000_nojump_nolanded.jsonl`.

Landed theorems used: the tail bound of the deficient leaves, through `defSound` and
`RankinTailGeneral`; nothing else beyond the engine.
-/

